  "working_thesis": "Hannah Arendt's The Human Condition undertakes a phenomenological reconsideration of the vita activa—divided into labor, work, and action—from the vantage point of modern experiences and fears, challenging traditional philosophical hierarchies, the rise of the social, and the consequences of earth and world alienation."
